{"c":[{"id":"ba466bbf79b5d07e","sum":"R3/G2: corpus event-card misses are producer code, not the router; context.ts reads 'unknown' selection as a caret. A goal is finished only with left[] empty; goal values are picked by their quoted part, not display.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"362f7f2441a3fcab","sum":"R3: corpus m36/m43 miss event cards by the producer's rule (relative date, no anchor), m37 finds no person: event-card code, not the router. routing/context.ts treats the helper's 'unknown' selection as a caret, since RouteFollower sends none then.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T170330Z-9c33f255f5c1caad","text":"R3: corpus m36/m43 list no event card by the producer's rule (a conversation line's relative date has no anchor); m37 finds no person. Those misses are event-card code, not the router.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T170330Z-dcc2d733c48b884a","text":"R3: RouteFollower sends no routingContext while the selection is a plain caret, so routing/context.ts treats the helper's 'unknown' selection as caret; comparing them ended every write session at the host's first sentence end.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"e516245b6d5f910e","sum":"G2: GoalProgress finished is done only with left[] empty; runs.ts owes every required or recipient field in windows a goal writes. A goal value's display names its source window, so goal-prompt.ts says pick values by their quoted part.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T173412Z-100b242cff553f5d","text":"G2: GoalProgress finished is done only when left[] is empty (partial/handoff otherwise); runs.ts owes every field left.ts marks required or recipient in windows a goal writes in, and a closed window leaves them unresolved.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T173412Z-33695164e4940cad","text":"G2: a goal value's display names its source window's title, so live qwen3.8 matched v.display.includes('ORD-...') to the sender's email; goal-prompt.ts now says pick values by their quoted part.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"6c61dbb360ed9d23","sum":"G2/L1: goal writes pass goals/gates.ts (lowerGoal async, needs askJev + ledger; desk tests use goal-desk.ts standInJev); never widen drafts.ts restates(); live Jev leaves D2-06 scene 2 partial; no chat route is a default (name groq:/gateway: via --dev-writer).","tree":{"c":[{"id":"8febf1c1fb5ea75f","sum":"G2: every goal write passes goals/gates.ts (never-typed, misfit, verifyWrites); with no Jev a goal writes no copied value (desk tests use goal-desk.ts standInJev). drafts.ts restates() is a closed-frame clause-suffix rule; never widen it by adding words.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T173412Z-c65516aec96de620","text":"G2: every goal write passes goals/gates.ts (never-typed, misfit + numberFieldMisfit, Ask's verifyWrites Jev question); lowerGoal is async and needs askJev + ledger; with no Jev a goal writes no copied value, so desk tests pass test/goal-desk.ts standInJev.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T173413Z-41b9cc8b0f0c0c83","text":"G2: drafts.ts restates() (skip Jev for a restated sentence) is a closed-frame clause-suffix rule; two reviews found 5 bypasses in looser versions (token sets, 'Avoid saying', 'NOT saying', 'provided'); never widen it by adding words.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"e10542c624d65f47","sum":"G2: live Jev (0.75 floor) confirmed Order number but not a reply's sender in To or a derived event, so D2-06 scene 2 ends partial live (evidence/screen/g2). L1: no chat route is a default; developers name groq:<model> or gateway:<model> via --dev-writer.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T180513Z-82a90a8786c261a8","text":"G2: live Jev (Ask's yes/no value question, 0.75 floor) confirmed Order number but not a reply's sender in To or a derived calendar event for 'add this meeting to my calendar and draft a reply to Priya', so D2-06 scene 2 ends partial live; see evidence/screen/g2 jev-*-probe.txt.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T201333Z-b3e261779dc6c92b","text":"L1: no chat route is a default (WRITER_ROUTE and INTENT_ROUTE null, ASK_MAKER jev); a developer names one as groq:<model> or gateway:<model> (writer/routes.ts) with the helper's --dev-writer or an eval script's writer flag.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
